  m_Name: Nation_Onondaga_(Haudenosaunee)
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Colonization.Runtime::Colonization.NativeNationData
  displayName: Onondaga (Haudenosaunee)
  leader: Garakontie
  date: c. 1660s
  biography: Garakontie was an Onondaga chief and important seventeenth-century diplomat. He represents Onondaga here, not an absolute monarch of all Haudenosaunee nations.
  region: Central present-day New York; Great Lakes and northeastern woodlands.
  terrain:
  - Broadleaf Forest
  - Mixed Forest
  - Prairie
  goods:
  - Food
  - Fur
  jobs:
  - Farmers
  - Fur Trappers
  rival: Wendat
  scenarioAggression: Medium
  contextNote: Wendat rivalry references seventeenth-century Haudenosaunee-Wendat conflicts; Garakontie's own career also included sustained peace negotiations.
  sources:
  - https://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/294
  - https://www.onondaganation.org/culture/homes/
